  {
   "id": 543779,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Use the graphs shown to determine whether the sequence of vertices <i>d</i> → <i>b</i> → <i>c</i> → <i>f</i> → <i>e</i> → <i>d</i> is a Hamilton cycle, an Euler circuit, both, or neither.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/3c85120970c633c2.png\" alt=\"Two graphs are labeled graph A and graph K. Graph A has five vertices: b, c, d, e, and f. Edges connect b c, c f, b d, b e, d e, and e f. Graph K has five vertices: m, n, o, p, and q. Edges connect m n, n o, n q, q o, o p, n p, and m p.\">\n",
